parts.text:
The root cause: AI SDK v6's `DefaultChatTransport` uses `EventSourceParserStream` and expects SSE-formatted JSON events. Our backend was sending the legacy `0:"..."` / `2:[...]` format which the parser doesn't recognize.

I've changed `orchestrator.py` to emit proper SSE events:

```
data: {"type":"start","messageId":"..."}
data: {"type":"start-step"}
data: {"type":"text-start","id":"text-0"}
data: {"type":"text-delta","id":"text-0","delta":"chunk"}
data: {"type":"text-end","id":"text-0"}
data: {"type":"data-citations","data":{...}}
data: {"type":"finish-step"}
data: {"type":"finish","finishReason":"stop"}
```

This matches the AI SDK v6 `uiMessageChunkSchema`. Run `make dev` again to rebuild with the fix. The backend should auto-restart via `--watch rebuild` when it detects the file change.

